          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which structure of the vulva is the developmental homologue of the scrotum?</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which structure of the vulva is the developmental homologue of the scrotum?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mons pubis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The mons pubis is a fatty pad overlying the pubic symphysis. It is not the scrotal homologue.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Labia minora</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The labia minora are thin, hairless folds rich in sebaceous glands. They do not correspond to the scrotum embryologically.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Labia majora</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct — the labia majora contain fat and smooth muscle, and develop from the labioscrotal swellings, the same embryological precursor as the scrotum.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Clitoris</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The clitoris (two corpora cavernosa converging at the glans) is the homologue of the penis, not the scrotum.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The labia majora correspond to the scrotum; both arise from the labioscrotal swellings. Remember the two pairs: labia majora ↔ scrotum, and clitoris ↔ penis."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The labia majora are the scrotal homologues, sharing origin from the labioscrotal swellings. The clitoris–penis pair is the other key genital homology to remember."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
