          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>During an IVF cycle, the embryologist plans to transfer the embryo at the blasto</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>During an IVF cycle, the embryologist plans to transfer the embryo at the blastocyst stage. Which structural feature confirms that the blastocyst stage has been reached?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>A solid mass of 16 or more blastomeres without a cavity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>That describes the morula (day 3–4). The morula must acquire a fluid-filled cavity before it qualifies as a blastocyst.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Formation of a fluid-filled cavity (blastocoel) within the cell mass</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct — the blastocoel appears around day 5 as fluid accumulates within the morula, marking the transition to the blastocyst stage.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Penetration of the trophoblast through the endometrial epithelium</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>That describes the onset of implantation (day 6–7), which occurs after the blastocyst has already formed and hatched from the zona pellucida.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Fusion of the two pronuclei within the fertilised oocyte</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Pronuclear fusion marks the completion of fertilisation (day 1), long before the blastocyst stage.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The blastocyst is defined by the blastocoel, a fluid-filled cavity forming around day 5 as fluid accumulates within the solid morula. This is the landmark embryologists use before transfer."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly. The blastocoel — a fluid-filled cavity — is the hallmark of the blastocyst (day 5). The morula (solid, 16+ cells, day 3–4) precedes it; implantation follows."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
